This PR fixes an issue where the base font size defined in tailwind.global.tw.css would take precedence over the font size `atomic-product-multi-value-text`, because it comes from a different component, atomic-product. Due to how constructed stylesheets get applied, we can't fix this by using css layers. Instead, we need to have the styles directly on the stylesheet of `atomic-product-multi-value-text`

This one is an interesting one, as it showcases how to migrate product template component styles from `template-system.pcss` to a component's stylesheet.

For most product template components, this change will be required first:
https://github.com/coveo/ui-kit/pull/5802/files#diff-913ab5c20cb2c3af53f6e5de776c7b0cd155ecfbae2b4fdf6e241cefee4c0a91

Then you can do something like:

```css
:host(.density-compact) {
  @apply text-sm;
}
:host(.density-normal) {
  @apply text-base;
}

```

Note that since `atomic-product-multi-value-text` has the same font size on all display modes/density settings, so we don't need to style differently based on those classes.

